{% set d = r.decision %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Bake-off decision pack · {{ r.program.name }}</title>
<style>
{% include "_style.css.j2" %}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Bake-off decision pack</div>
    <h1>{{ r.program.name }}</h1>
    <div class="meta">Trial {{ r.trial.start }} to {{ r.trial.end }} ({{ r.trial.weeks }} weeks) · {{ r.vendors | length }} vendors · {{ r.trial.control_teams }} control teams · teams assigned by lottery</div>
  </div>
  <div class="grade word {{ '' if d.clear else 'c-medium' }}" title="Decision"><div><b>{{ d.winner or (d.leader ~ "?" if d.leader else "None") }}</b><small>{{ "Clear winner" if d.clear else "No clear winner" }}</small></div></div>
</header>

<p class="headline">{{ d.text }}</p>

<h2><span class="num">1</span>Performance against the control teams</h2>
<p>Each vendor's teams were compared with the control teams over the same weeks, with the same estimator, guardrails and team-level ranges as any evidence pack. Negative means less time per ticket.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Vendor</th><th class="n">Teams</th><th>Grade</th><th class="n">Change</th><th class="n">95% range</th><th>Guardrails</th><th class="n">Claims that did not hold</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for v in r.vendors %}<tr>
  <td><b>{{ v.vendor }}</b></td><td class="n">{{ v.teams }}</td>
  {% if v.error %}<td colspan="5">Could not be measured: {{ v.error }}</td>
  {% else %}
  <td>{{ v.grade }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.relative | spct(1) }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.relative_ci_low | spct(1) }} to {{ v.relative_ci_high | spct(1) }}</td>
  <td>{% if v.blocked %}<span class="chip chip-breach">Breached</span>{% else %}<span class="chip chip-pass">Held</span>{% endif %}</td>
  <td class="n">{% if v.audit %}{{ v.audit.failed_share.estimate | pct }} ({{ v.audit.failed_share.ci_low | pct }} to {{ v.audit.failed_share.ci_high | pct }}){% else %}n/a{% endif %}</td>
  {% endif %}
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>

{% if r.vendors | selectattr("annual_price") | list %}
<h2><span class="num">2</span>Value for money</h2>
<p>Hours released and their capacity value, scaled from the trial to a year, against each vendor's quoted price. Capacity is not cash: see each vendor's evidence for how much would turn into savings.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Vendor</th><th class="n">Hours a year</th><th class="n">Capacity value a year</th><th class="n">Quoted price a year</th><th class="n">Net</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for v in r.vendors if not v.error %}<tr><td>{{ v.vendor }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.annual_hours | num(0) }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.annual_capacity_value | money }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.annual_price | money }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.net_annual_value | money }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}

<h2><span class="num">3</span>How to read this</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A vendor is eligible only if its effect excludes zero, its evidence grade counts and no quality guardrail breached.</li>
  <li>The leader is clearly ahead only if its range does not overlap the runner-up's. That test is conservative: a real but small difference can still read as "no clear winner".</li>
  <li>With a no-clear-winner result, decide on price and contract terms, or extend the trial; the measurement plan shows how many weeks more would separate them.</li>
</ul>
{% if r.notes %}<ul>{% for n in r.notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
<p class="meta">Probative Labs {{ r.lineage.code.probative }} · configuration <span class="mono">{{ r.lineage.config_sha256[:12] }}</span> · run {{ r.lineage.run_at }}</p>
<footer>Generated by Probative Labs, independent verification of what AI delivers. Vendors did not run or grade this trial. Method: docs/bakeoff.md.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
